# Line-ending contract.
#
# Shell scripts, hooks and templates MUST use LF. CRLF any of them and:
#   - shebangs become `#!/bin/sh\r` -> "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M"
#   - `hooks/*` are copied verbatim into .git/hooks/ by install-git-hooks.sh,
#     so a CRLF source hook installs a broken hook
#   - anchored greps (e.g. `^AGENT_OS_SOURCE=<path>$`) fail on the trailing \r
#
# Deliberately NOT blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`: this framework deploys files
# into consumer repos, and forcing LF on all consumer text (lockfiles, future
# *.bat/*.ps1, project files) is a behaviour change they never opted into.
# The explicit globs below cover every file class with a known CRLF hazard.
# Verify with: bash scripts/framework-verify.sh  (LF guard section)

*.sh           text eol=lf
*.bash         text eol=lf
*.py           text eol=lf
hooks/*        text eol=lf
templates/**   text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
.editorconfig  text eol=lf
